      "role": "user",
      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\n- ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\n\n## Column Mapping\n- academic year: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- academic year description: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC\n- department name: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- total coefficient of variation: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- current term: ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.IS_CURRENT_TERM\n- total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS\n- degree-granting departments: SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- Chemistry (Course 5): SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- average total units: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS\n- range: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS\n- variance: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS\n- 2008 academic year: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n\n## Join Keys\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE <-> COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE <-> ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_CODE\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"math\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"degree-granting\" is predicated by \"TABLE.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'\"\n- \"Course 18\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"Chemistry\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '5'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each academic year, what is the academic year description and the coefficient of variation of the total units for all subjects offered in terms that are marked as the current term in the term parameter table and are offered by the Mathematics department (Course 18)?\n```sql\nSELECT aca.ACADEMIC_YEAR, aca.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, STDDEV(sub.TOTAL_UNITS)/NULLIF(AVG(sub.TOTAL_UNITS),0) AS coefficient_of_variation FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED sub JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL aca ON sub.TERM_CODE = aca.TERM_CODE JOIN ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER param ON aca.TERM_CODE = param.TERM_CODE WHERE param.IS_CURRENT_TERM = 'Y' AND sub.TOTAL_UNITS > 0 AND sub.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' GROUP BY aca.ACADEMIC_YEAR, aca.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC HAVING AVG(sub.TOTAL_UNITS) > 0 ORDER BY coefficient_of_variation DESC;\n```\n2. For each department, provide the department's name and calculate the range and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2008 academic year, but only include departments that are degree-granting and exclude the Chemistry department (Course 5).\n```sql\nSELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, MAX(ccc.TOTAL_UNITS) - MIN(ccc.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_range, VARIANCE(ccc.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_variance FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT sd JOIN CIS_COURSE_CATALOG ccc ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = ccc.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND ccc.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2008 AND sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '5' GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n```\n3. For each academic year, what is the academic year description, and for each department, what is the coefficient of variation of the total units for all subjects offered in terms that are marked as the current term in the term parameter table? For each academic year, also include a grand total for all departments in the format of (academic year, academic year description, null, total coefficient of variation).\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT aca.ACADEMIC_YEAR, aca.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, sub.DEPARTMENT_NAME, STDDEV(sub.TOTAL_UNITS)/NULLIF(AVG(sub.TOTAL_UNITS),0) AS coefficient_of_variation FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED sub JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL aca ON sub.TERM_CODE = aca.TERM_CODE JOIN ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER param ON aca.TERM_CODE = param.TERM_CODE WHERE param.IS_CURRENT_TERM = 'Y' AND sub.TOTAL_UNITS > 0 GROUP BY aca.ACADEMIC_YEAR, aca.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, sub.DEPARTMENT_NAME HAVING AVG(sub.TOTAL_UNITS) > 0 ) SELECT ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, DEPARTMENT_NAME, SUM(coefficient_of_variation) AS total_coefficient_of_variation FROM inner_cte GROUP BY ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, DEPARTMENT_NAME WITH ROLLUP HAVING SUM(coefficient_of_variation) > 0 ORDER BY ACADEMIC_YEAR, DEPARTMENT_NAME ;\n```\n4. Among all degree-granting departments except Chemistry (Course 5), which department had the highest average total units for subjects offered in the 2008 academic year, and what is the range and variance of total units for subjects in that department?\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE, MAX(ccc.TOTAL_UNITS) - MIN(ccc.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_range, VARIANCE(ccc.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_variance, AVG(ccc.TOTAL_UNITS) AS avg_total_units FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT sd JOIN CIS_COURSE_CATALOG ccc ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = ccc.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND ccc.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2008 AND sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '5' GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE ) SELECT ic.DEPARTMENT_NAME, ic.avg_total_units, ic.total_units_range, ic.total_units_variance FROM inner_cte ic WHERE ic.avg_total_units = ( SELECT MAX(avg_total_units) FROM inner_cte )\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each academic year, what is the academic year, academic year description, department name, the total coefficient of variation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for all subjects offered in terms marked as the current term, and for the department (among all degree-granting departments except Chemistry (Course 5)) with the highest average total units for subjects offered in the 2008 academic year, also include the average total units, the range, and the variance of total units for subjects in that department? For each academic year, also include a grand total for all departments in the format of (academic year, academic year description, null, total coefficient of variation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), null, null, null). Do not return any rounded answers."
