      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database connection is persistently unavailable (authentication error `1045` on every attempt, including `SELECT 1`), so runtime verification is impossible. I will complete the investigation based on the semantic network evidence and the provided gold decomposition, which are fully consistent with the retrieved table/column definitions.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (all retrieved via `semantic_get`):**\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — catalog-level attributes of each subject offered per academic year/term. Key columns: `TERM_CODE` (joins term tables), `DEPARTMENT_NAME` (e.g. 'Mathematics'), `TOTAL_UNITS` (total credit units), `ACADEMIC_YEAR`. Granularity: one row per subject offering per term/academic year.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL** — extended term dimension (superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS). Key columns: `TERM_CODE`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC`. Does not carry IS_REGULAR_TERM/TERM_STATUS.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER** — exactly three rows resolving relative term references (current/previous/upcoming). Key columns: `TERM_CODE`, `IS_CURRENT_TERM` ('Y'/'N'), `TERM_INDICATOR`.\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY** — subject-level rollup of section offerings per term; carries `OFFER_DEPT_CODE` (joins SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE), `TOTAL_UNITS`, enrollment numbers.\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** — department dimension: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` ('Y'/'N'), school attribution.\n- **CIS_COURSE_CATALOG** — alternative CIS catalog feed with same attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED; keyed by `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `TERM_CODE`, subject identity; carries `DEPARTMENT_CODE` (joins SIS_DEPARTMENT) and `TOTAL_UNITS`.\n\n**Column concepts:** `column_concept_total_units` (TOTAL_UNITS replicated across catalog/registrar tables; decision guide: catalog unit statistics → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS), `column_concept_term_code` (universal term join key; \"current term\" resolution → ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER), `column_concept_department_name` (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME conventions; code joins preferred for dimension attributes), `column_concept_year_columns` (academic vs fiscal vs aid year systems).\n\n**Concepts:** `concept_academic_term_dimension` (ACADEMIC_TERMS vs ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL vs ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER coverage/roles), `concept_course_catalog_sources` (warehouse vs CIS vs Drupal catalog feeds), `concept_subject_offering_facts`, `concept_department_dimension`.\n\n**Metrics (precedents):** dw_1393, dw_2597, dw_41, dw_1023, dw_1335, dw_2180, dw_1049, dw_2151, dw_2272, dw_1212, dw_1301, dw_3417, dw_4701, dw_3644, dw_2958, dw_4640, dw_3311, dw_3530, dw_1471, dw_4527, dw_4325, dw_2158, dw_3356, dw_3280, dw_2461, dw_4061, dw_3664, dw_3248, dw_3609, dw_3078, dw_2335, dw_4812, dw_3867, dw_359, dw_2850, dw_4231, dw_1758, dw_4911, dw_2181, dw_1288, dw_3493, dw_4387, dw_2377, dw_3904, dw_2628, dw_4305, dw_1302, dw_3163, dw_2924, dw_1766, dw_2210, dw_1427, dw_3901, dw_3294, dw_4756, dw_2398, dw_5150, dw_3042, dw_4405, dw_3237, dw_2580, dw_1692, dw_5103, dw_4234, dw_3727, dw_3985, dw_3498, dw_4130, dw_3668, dw_2559, dw_3273, dw_3867 — all consume the same table family for unit-statistics question shapes.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\nFrom `semantic_graph` on COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: outgoing joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS, ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, SIS_DEPARTMENT, FCLT_ROOMS, EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY, CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE, SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE; incoming joins from SUBJECT_SUMMARY, TIP_DETAIL/TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL, SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG. Concept memberships: concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_course_catalog_sources. Column-concept memberships: term_code, subject_id, department_name, total_units, year_columns, hass_attribute.\n\nDocumented join keys (hint + column definitions agree): ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE ↔ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE; ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE ↔ ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_CODE; SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE ↔ CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.DEPARTMENT_CODE; SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE ↔ SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_CODE.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (catalog/term candidates):**\n\n| Dimension | COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED | CIS_COURSE_CATALOG | SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY | ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL | ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | subject offering per term/year (evidence: `default_granularity`) | subject per term in CIS feed | subject per term (registrar rollup) | one row per term | 3 rows total |\n| TOTAL_UNITS | yes (catalog-declared) | yes (CIS copy) | yes (registrar value) | n/a | n/a |\n| ACADEMIC_YEAR | own column | own column (used for \"2008 academic year\" filter) | none (via term join) | yes + ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC | none |\n| DEPARTMENT_NAME | yes | yes (plus DEPARTMENT_CODE) | OFFER_DEPT_NAME/OFFER_DEPT_CODE | n/a | n/a |\n| Current-term resolution | via TERM_CODE join | via TERM_CODE | via TERM_CODE | IS_CURRENT_TERM flag exists but hint anchors \"current term\" to parameter table | IS_CURRENT_TERM authoritative (3-row reference) |\n\nEvidence: `column_concept_total_units` comparisons (source process differs: catalog-declared vs registrar); `concept_academic_term_dimension` decision_guide (\"current term\" → ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER); `concept_course_catalog_sources` (CIS feed used with ACADEMIC_YEAR keying).\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- CV of TOTAL_UNITS per academic year × department, current-term filter: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED + ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL + ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER — SUPPORTED (all columns exist; hint subquery 3 is the exact precedent).\n- Grand-total row per academic year with NULL department: SUPPORTED via `GROUP BY ... WITH ROLLUP` (hint subquery 3).\n- Top degree-granting (≠ Course 5) department by AVG(TOTAL_UNITS) in ACADEMIC_YEAR 2008, with range/variance: SIS_DEPARTMENT + CIS_COURSE_CATALOG — SUPPORTED (`IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`, `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `TOTAL_UNITS` all exist; hint subqueries 2/4 are exact precedents). SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY — NOT-SUPPORTED for the 2008 filter (no ACADEMIC_YEAR column).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"terms marked as the current term\" → ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.IS_CURRENT_TERM = 'Y' (hint column mapping; concept decision_guide). \"academic year / academic year description\" → ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR / ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC. \"degree-granting\" → SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y' (domain knowledge). \"Chemistry (Course 5)\" → DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '5' (domain knowledge). \"2008 academic year\" → CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2008 (hint mapping). \"total coefficient of variation\" → STDDEV(TOTAL_UNITS)/AVG(TOTAL_UNITS) summed per group (hint mapping anchors it to COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS).\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** CV-of-TOTAL_UNITS precedents: dw_2180, dw_4640 (on COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED). Range/variance of TOTAL_UNITS for 2008 degree-granting departments precedents: dw_1335 (CIS_COURSE_CATALOG-based 'Math 2008 Stats' branch). WITH ROLLUP grand-total precedents: dw_1288, dw_3904, dw_1302, dw_1427, dw_4234. Two-level \"top department by average\" precedent: hint subquery 4 shape matches dw_2272/dw_2151 family.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\nCOURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED is the default catalog source for unit statistics (decision_guide of column_concept_total_units and concept_course_catalog_sources); it is consumed by dozens of metrics (dw_41, dw_1023, dw_2180, dw_359, etc.). ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL supplies academic-year attributes over the widest term coverage; ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER resolves relative term references. SIS_DEPARTMENT provides the degree-granting flag used in department-scope filters (dw_1393, dw_2151, dw_4527). CIS_COURSE_CATALOG serves year-keyed catalog analyses joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT by code (dw_1335, dw_2210). SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY serves registrar-side subject rollups with enrollment; it is listed among gold tables and joins SIS_DEPARTMENT via OFFER_DEPT_CODE, but the task's measure/filter columns are all satisfied without it.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: semantic_get ✓, semantic_graph query_neighbors ✓\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL: semantic_get ✓, graph via neighbors of CCSO ✓\n- ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER: semantic_get ✓\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY: semantic_get ✓\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT: semantic_get ✓\n- CIS_COURSE_CATALOG: semantic_get ✓, graph (incoming join edge to CCSO) ✓\n- column_concept_total_units / term_code / department_name / year_columns: semantic_get ✓\n- concept_academic_term_dimension / concept_course_catalog_sources: semantic_get ✓\n- Metric precedents (dw_1335, dw_2180, dw_1288, dw_2272, dw_2151, dw_1393, etc.): retrieved via semantic_search descriptions ✓\n- mysql_query verification: **attempted 8 times; all failed with server-side authentication error 1045 (database unavailable in this session)** — noted explicitly rather than guessed.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:** COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (TOTAL_UNITS, DEPARTMENT_NAME, TERM_CODE) joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC) and ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER (IS_CURRENT_TERM='Y') for the per-year/per-department CV with WITH ROLLUP grand totals; SIS_DEPARTMENT (IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y', DEPARTMENT_CODE<>'5') joined to CIS_COURSE_CATALOG (ACADEMIC_YEAR=2008, TOTAL_UNITS) for the top-average department's avg/range/variance, attached via LEFT JOIN on department name.\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** two CTEs mirroring hint subqueries 3 and 4; inner CTE computes per-(year, dept) CV with `TOTAL_UNITS > 0` and `HAVING AVG > 0`; rollup CTE sums CVs `WITH ROLLUP` (dept-level rows plus per-year grand-total rows with NULL department); top-dept CTE selects the max-average department; final LEFT JOIN attaches avg/range/variance only to the matching department row (NULL for all other rows and for grand-total rows, exactly as the requested format specifies). Bare `STDDEV()` used per the tip. No rounding applied.\n\n**6c. Reasons:** *Data* — all required columns physically exist per retrieved definitions; TERM_CODE joins are documented 1:1 dimension joins (no fan-out; ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER contributes only its single current-term row). *Semantic-network* — concept_academic_term_dimension decision_guide mandates ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER for \"current term\"; column_concept_total_units decision_guide mandates COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS for catalog unit statistics; hint join keys confirm SIS_DEPARTMENT↔CIS_COURSE_CATALOG on DEPARTMENT_CODE. *Business* — dw_2180/dw_4640 (CV precedents), dw_1335 (2008 range/variance precedent), dw_1288/dw_3904 (ROLLUP grand-total precedents) all use this exact table/column combination.\n\n**6d. Alternatives:** SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY could theoretically supply TOTAL_UNITS, but it lacks ACADEMIC_YEAR and catalog-attribute parity, and no hint subquery uses it for measures — rejected. Database execution verification was impossible (persistent auth error); the query follows the verified gold decomposition exactly.\n\n",
